I implemented the node, but not the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so:

- **Log file:** appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem authority, which the node doesn't have.
- **Metadata fetch:** calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which isn't granted. Sending the input's text to an external service would also go beyond what the node is allowed to do.

If operations wants either, the graph's `with` clause has to grant the matching capability first (for example a logging or `http-client` handle scoped to that host).

The store key `urls` is my assumption, since the spec doesn't name the key. The value is read as newline-separated URLs, and blank lines are dropped.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = state_read::get("urls")
            .map(|raw| {
                raw.lines()
                    .map(|l| l.trim())
                    .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                    .map(|l| l.to_string())
                    .collect::<Vec<String>>()
            })
            .unwrap_or_default();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

